\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\kerning2\b\f0\fs44\lang16393 GENERATIVE AI\par
\b0\fs24 Generative AI (Artificial Intelligence) is a type of AI that can create new content such as text, images, music, videos, and computer code by learning patterns from large amounts of existing data.\par
Unlike traditional AI, which mainly analyzes data or makes predictions, generative AI can generate original outputs that resemble human-created content.\par
At the core of generative AI are advanced machine learning models, particularly \b Large Language Models (LLMs)\b0  and \b deep neural networks\b0 . These models are trained on vast amounts of data and learn how different pieces of information relate to one another. Once trained, they can produce new outputs that are often difficult to distinguish from content created by humans.\par
One of the most significant breakthroughs in generative AI is its ability to understand and respond to natural language. Tools such as chatbots and AI assistants can answer questions, summarize documents, draft emails, create reports, and even assist with complex problem-solving. In addition to text generation, modern generative AI systems can create realistic artwork, compose music, generate videos, and write software code from simple instructions.\par
As AI models continue to improve, generative AI is expected to become an integral part of everyday life and work. Rather than replacing humans, it is often viewed as a powerful tool that augments human creativity, productivity, and decision-making. Its ability to generate content, solve problems, and assist users interactively makes it one of the most influential technological advancements of the modern era.\par
Generative AI is trained on vast datasets and uses advanced machine learning models, particularly Large Language Models (LLMs) and deep learning neural networks, to understand patterns and produce new content.\par
\par
\b\fs40 Types of Generative AI\par
\b0\fs28 Generative AI systems are designed to create different forms of content. Depending on the type of data they process and generate, they can be classified into several categories.\par
